WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:00.965
- Hey guys it's Justine

00:00:00.965 --> 00:00:02.855
and the Apple event just ended

00:00:02.855 --> 00:00:05.223
and I'm so hyped up about

00:00:05.223 --> 00:00:06.863
the iPad Pros that,

00:00:06.863 --> 00:00:07.927
oh my goodness,

00:00:07.927 --> 00:00:09.416
I was freaking out at my desk,

00:00:09.416 --> 00:00:10.600
I probably should've filmed,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.410
I did film this clip whenever I heard

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.433
that the new iPad Pro will have USBC

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:18.711
and it will charge your iPhone.

00:00:18.711 --> 00:00:20.169
- [Announcer] We now support charging out

00:00:20.169 --> 00:00:22.746
over USBC so you can
even charge your iPhone

00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:23.648
unlike any other tablet.

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:26.909
(applause)
(body falling)

00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:28.081
- Anyway I just wanted to go through

00:00:28.081 --> 00:00:29.358
a little recap of some of the things

00:00:29.358 --> 00:00:30.416
that they announced today.

00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:32.419
Three of the main things
that they highlighted

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:33.865
was the new Mac Mini,

00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:34.881
the new MacBook Air,

00:00:34.881 --> 00:00:36.515
and of course the iPad Pros.

00:00:36.515 --> 00:00:38.294
Angela also announced 60 new sessions

00:00:38.294 --> 00:00:40.513
at Apple retail stores which
I was really excited about

00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:42.501
because Zach King has a session.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.260
So they co-create sessions with people

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.971
and I'm such a huge fan of his.

00:00:45.971 --> 00:00:48.020
I used to love all of his
Vines that he would post,

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.993
and now since Vine is no longer a thing

00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:52.132
I love all of the things
that he posted on YouTube,

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:53.585
and all of the things on Twitter,

00:00:53.585 --> 00:00:56.003
so congratulations Zach I am so excited

00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:58.396
I will definitely be taking
one of those sessions.

00:00:58.396 --> 00:00:59.410
Now let's talk about some of the things

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.854
that they covered in the keynote.

00:01:00.854 --> 00:01:02.982
First up, we're gonna
chat about the MacBook Air

00:01:02.982 --> 00:01:05.147
because I remember the time

00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:07.538
that Steve Jobs pulled
that first MacBook Air

00:01:07.538 --> 00:01:10.985
out of that envelope and it was shocking.

00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:14.539
- Today we're introducing
a third kind of notebook,

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:16.143
called the MacBook Air.

00:01:16.143 --> 00:01:18.393
(applause)

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.046
- One of the smallest laptops
that Apple had ever created

00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:24.315
up until that point.

00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:25.790
So for me I was like,

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.504
this is exciting.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.548
Now it was exciting but
for somebody who does

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:32.161
video editing and very
processor intensive things

00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:35.387
this laptop did not quite deliver.

00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:37.877
For what it was I did
use it a lot for email

00:01:37.877 --> 00:01:40.043
and I was able to edit very small files

00:01:40.043 --> 00:01:42.326
but even then it just
didn't have enough power

00:01:42.326 --> 00:01:43.341
to be able to do the things

00:01:43.341 --> 00:01:44.976
that I really needed it to do.

00:01:44.976 --> 00:01:46.364
So here they are they
come in the three colors

00:01:46.364 --> 00:01:48.037
you have the silver, the rose gold,

00:01:48.037 --> 00:01:49.842
and of course the space gray.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.137
It has an all new Retina screen

00:01:51.137 --> 00:01:53.903
with four times the resolution
as the previous Air.

00:01:53.903 --> 00:01:56.339
During the keynote when Tim
said something about like,

00:01:56.339 --> 00:01:58.576
this is something that
everyone has always wanted,

00:01:58.576 --> 00:02:01.269
I tweeted, a touch screen MacBook?

00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:02.923
Then two seconds later he said

00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:05.083
a retina display!
(laughter)

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:06.453
And I tweeted, oh.

00:02:06.453 --> 00:02:07.409
This is definitely something

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.938
that I think was needed on
the MacBook Airs because

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:12.180
when you're using the Retina
displays and then you go back

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.920
to using something that isn't a Retina

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.489
it's extremely hard for
your eyes to adjust.

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:18.015
So I'm sure this display looks amazing

00:02:18.015 --> 00:02:19.754
and I can't wait to get
a chance to check it out.

00:02:19.754 --> 00:02:22.436
It has an all new eighth
gen dual core CPU,

00:02:22.436 --> 00:02:23.458
16 gigs of RAM,

00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:25.380
1.5 terabyte solid state drive,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.215
and these drives are 60% faster
than the previous versions.

00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:30.046
Another huge upgrade to the MacBook Air

00:02:30.046 --> 00:02:31.042
is the touch ID.

00:02:31.042 --> 00:02:33.313
It still has the FaceTime
camera at the top,

00:02:33.313 --> 00:02:35.472
they did update the
keyboard and the track pad

00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:37.160
so it does have the butterfly keyboard

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.937
and the force touch track pad.

00:02:38.937 --> 00:02:40.118
They also gave the speakers an update

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:42.144
so they're 25% louder which is good

00:02:42.144 --> 00:02:44.367
because I do feel like the
MacBook Air, if I recall

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.566
I haven't used them in a really long time,

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.960
the speakers definitely weren't as loud

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.121
as some of the MacBooks.

00:02:49.121 --> 00:02:51.491
It's a 1/4 pound lighter than
the previous MacBook Air.

00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:54.363
So this thing weighs in at 2.75 pounds.

00:02:54.363 --> 00:02:56.031
The prices start at $1199

00:02:56.031 --> 00:02:58.886
and one of the huge things
that they seemed to stress

00:02:58.886 --> 00:03:00.334
during this entire Apple Keynote is

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.467
their MacBooks, their
Mac Minis, and the iPads

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.134
are all recyclable aluminum.

00:03:04.134 --> 00:03:06.281
So I feel like that
got some of the loudest

00:03:06.281 --> 00:03:07.451
cheers in the audience,

00:03:07.451 --> 00:03:08.386
and I think it's really great

00:03:08.386 --> 00:03:10.372
because there are so many
products that we're using.

00:03:10.372 --> 00:03:12.340
So just to know that
you're using something

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.327
that has been recycled
is a pretty cool thing.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:17.024
Now let's move on to the Mac Mini,

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:19.634
it is an all new space gray color.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:20.569
This thing kinda just looks like

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:22.617
a big Apple TV sort of but

00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:24.024
with the space gray finish.

00:03:24.024 --> 00:03:27.382
I haven't used a Mac Mini
in a really long time.

00:03:27.382 --> 00:03:28.764
I personally probably won't be using

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:30.581
a Mac Mini but they do look incredible

00:03:30.581 --> 00:03:32.839
and after they showed
this server farm photo

00:03:32.839 --> 00:03:36.160
I had a lot of ideas of
things that I wanted to do.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.983
Do I need a Mac Mini farm?

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:40.335
I don't know maybe, do you?

00:03:40.335 --> 00:03:42.572
Realistically I probably
won't be getting a Mac Mini

00:03:42.572 --> 00:03:44.080
as something that I will use everyday

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.179
because I do have an iMac
Pro, and my MacBook Pro

00:03:46.179 --> 00:03:48.197
that I edit and do most of my work on.

00:03:48.197 --> 00:03:50.267
This Mac Mini upgrade was a huge upgrade

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.402
from the previous one.

00:03:51.402 --> 00:03:52.646
Starting at four cores

00:03:52.646 --> 00:03:54.229
you can go all the way up to six,

00:03:54.229 --> 00:03:55.883
with 60% faster graphics,

00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:57.776
that's five times faster than before

00:03:57.776 --> 00:04:00.046
and you can upgrade up to 64 gigs of RAM.

00:04:00.046 --> 00:04:02.235
And a solid state drive up to 2 terabytes.

00:04:02.235 --> 00:04:03.501
One of the things that Apple is known for

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.263
is removing ports but they did not do that

00:04:05.263 --> 00:04:06.113
with the Mac Mini.

00:04:06.113 --> 00:04:08.693
It has four thunderbolt, three USBC ports,

00:04:08.693 --> 00:04:12.595
HDMI, two USBA ports, 10
gigabyte ethernet port,

00:04:12.595 --> 00:04:15.030
all available starting November 7th.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.807
The starting price for
one of the Mac Minis

00:04:16.807 --> 00:04:18.372
is $799 and that will get you

00:04:18.372 --> 00:04:19.265
eight gigs of RAM,

00:04:19.265 --> 00:04:21.705
3.6 gigahertz quad core processor,

00:04:21.705 --> 00:04:23.984
with 128 gigs of storage.

00:04:23.984 --> 00:04:25.756
So the most expensive Mac Mini,

00:04:25.756 --> 00:04:26.928
let's spec this out.

00:04:26.928 --> 00:04:28.559
3.2 gigahertz,

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:29.733
six core,

00:04:29.733 --> 00:04:32.276
we would like the 64 gigs of RAM,

00:04:32.276 --> 00:04:34.752
2 terabyte solid state storage,

00:04:34.752 --> 00:04:36.772
of course we're going to upgrade

00:04:36.772 --> 00:04:39.905
our 10 gigabyte ethernet port,

00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:42.254
and I guess we don't
need Final Cut or Logic.

00:04:42.254 --> 00:04:43.584
So let's add this to our bag.

00:04:43.584 --> 00:04:46.334
That gives us a total of $4, 199.

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:50.018
Well we might as well add AppleCare on.

00:04:50.018 --> 00:04:51.390
I think that the Mac Minis are great,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.935
I think that this a perfect
thing for a lot of people

00:04:53.935 --> 00:04:55.214
and there are so many different use cases.

00:04:55.214 --> 00:04:56.616
It's so small it's so compact,

00:04:56.616 --> 00:04:58.466
and I have been a really
big fan of the Mac Minis

00:04:58.466 --> 00:04:59.606
since the beginning and when they

00:04:59.606 --> 00:05:00.596
first announced these things,

00:05:00.596 --> 00:05:01.942
this is kind of crazy,

00:05:01.942 --> 00:05:03.794
I did actually get one.

00:05:03.794 --> 00:05:04.827
There were all of these give aways

00:05:04.827 --> 00:05:06.290
that they used to do on Myspace

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.678
and I managed to win
one in some give away.

00:05:08.678 --> 00:05:10.241
I don't even want to, we
don't have to go there.

00:05:10.241 --> 00:05:11.621
That's for another day.

00:05:11.621 --> 00:05:13.830
But I was in, I think I was in college,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.385
and I was so excited cause it was like

00:05:15.385 --> 00:05:18.326
Yes a free Mac Mini my life is complete!

00:05:18.326 --> 00:05:20.486
So that's Mac Mini, now let's
talk about the iPad Pro.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.803
Wow, wow.

00:05:21.803 --> 00:05:24.017
This thing looks beautiful,

00:05:24.017 --> 00:05:25.207
and I'm gonna be
completely honest with you,

00:05:25.207 --> 00:05:27.438
I do have one of the first gen iPad Pros

00:05:27.438 --> 00:05:29.010
and I don't really use it that often.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.853
I use my phone, I use my MacBook,

00:05:30.853 --> 00:05:31.940
and if I'm not using one of those

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.537
I'm on my desktop iMac Pro.

00:05:33.537 --> 00:05:36.024
But it really is my dream
to just have one device.

00:05:36.024 --> 00:05:38.303
If I just had one device
that could do everything,

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:39.835
that would be so incredible,

00:05:39.835 --> 00:05:41.202
especially for traveling.

00:05:41.202 --> 00:05:42.969
I feel like the iPad Pro is getting

00:05:42.969 --> 00:05:44.469
closer and closer to that.

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:46.921
Especially with all kinds
of new editing software

00:05:46.921 --> 00:05:47.754
that's coming out.

00:05:47.754 --> 00:05:49.435
I just wish that Final Cut or iMovie

00:05:49.435 --> 00:05:51.981
would have an upgraded app on the iPhone.

00:05:51.981 --> 00:05:52.814
It doesn't make sense,

00:05:52.814 --> 00:05:54.446
like you guys have the resources

00:05:54.446 --> 00:05:57.930
to make the most perfect
editing app on your iPhone

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.456
and the iPad and yet
Adobe went and did it?

00:06:01.456 --> 00:06:03.934
You've got the resources,
you've already got Final Cut

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:05.208
you have iMovie on here,

00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:07.644
there's so many things that
you guys could be doing,

00:06:07.644 --> 00:06:09.139
that it makes me just want to

00:06:09.139 --> 00:06:11.232
take this desk and push it over

00:06:11.232 --> 00:06:13.482
knowing that it's possible.

00:06:14.425 --> 00:06:16.035
I just want to have that seamless solution

00:06:16.035 --> 00:06:17.446
to be able to have the capabilities

00:06:17.446 --> 00:06:20.486
of things that I can do on
Final Cut or iMovie on my phone.

00:06:20.486 --> 00:06:21.957
Like vertical video editing?

00:06:21.957 --> 00:06:24.401
You'd think that would be a no brainer.

00:06:24.401 --> 00:06:25.436
Thankfully Adobe Rush,

00:06:25.436 --> 00:06:27.875
I've actually been a
really huge fan of it.

00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:29.263
I don't edit in Premier,

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:30.705
I do edit everything in Final Cut,

00:06:30.705 --> 00:06:32.362
so I was a little bit
hesitant to check it out.

00:06:32.362 --> 00:06:35.334
But the Adobe Rush app
is really, really good.

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:37.925
After I tweeted about that
a lot of you guys suggested

00:06:37.925 --> 00:06:39.826
that I check out Luma Fusion,

00:06:39.826 --> 00:06:41.879
and I still haven't
actually checked it out

00:06:41.879 --> 00:06:43.053
so that is on my too do list.

00:06:43.053 --> 00:06:44.582
If you have used Luma Fusion

00:06:44.582 --> 00:06:45.525
let me know what you guys think of it.

00:06:45.525 --> 00:06:46.605
Or if you've used Adobe Rush,

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:47.879
or if there are any other features

00:06:47.879 --> 00:06:49.739
that you wish that there were

00:06:49.739 --> 00:06:51.954
video editing capabilities
built into the phone.

00:06:51.954 --> 00:06:53.981
I feel like a lot of these
things could be built

00:06:53.981 --> 00:06:55.346
right into the camera app.

00:06:55.346 --> 00:06:56.554
That is just a future wish,

00:06:56.554 --> 00:06:57.832
and I'm hoping that that is something

00:06:57.832 --> 00:06:58.849
that they are working on

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:01.695
because if they are you will see me doing,

00:07:01.695 --> 00:07:03.667
well maybe I'll dance
at the Apple store again

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:04.500
to celebrate.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.007
iPad Pro, they also
announced an Apple Pencil 2.

00:07:08.007 --> 00:07:09.363
It has gesture control,

00:07:09.363 --> 00:07:11.057
and I also got mine engraved.

00:07:11.057 --> 00:07:12.848
Again, I'm not an illustrator

00:07:12.848 --> 00:07:14.380
I don't really do that many things

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.684
on the iPad that would
require the Apple Pencil.

00:07:16.684 --> 00:07:18.537
They also showed a full version

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:20.851
of the new Adobe app for iPad

00:07:20.851 --> 00:07:22.906
and it looks extremely powerful which

00:07:22.906 --> 00:07:24.297
I'm also excited about.

00:07:24.297 --> 00:07:25.655
That's why I also tweeted that

00:07:25.655 --> 00:07:26.719
we're getting closer and closer

00:07:26.719 --> 00:07:28.456
to having an iPad be something

00:07:28.456 --> 00:07:29.476
that you can travel with

00:07:29.476 --> 00:07:31.120
and that can be your main device.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.352
So here it is this is,
aw, it is so beautiful,

00:07:34.352 --> 00:07:36.504
so it has rounded corners on the display,

00:07:36.504 --> 00:07:37.337
and they said that they're using

00:07:37.337 --> 00:07:38.236
some of the same technologies

00:07:38.236 --> 00:07:40.335
that they used in the iPhone 10 R

00:07:40.335 --> 00:07:41.608
with the liquid Retina display.

00:07:41.608 --> 00:07:43.143
A 12.9 inch display,

00:07:43.143 --> 00:07:45.229
it's 5.9 mm thick

00:07:45.229 --> 00:07:46.764
and this is 15% thinner

00:07:46.764 --> 00:07:50.545
then the previous iPad
Pro which was 6.9 inches.

00:07:50.545 --> 00:07:54.275
It also has Face ID which
means no home button.

00:07:54.275 --> 00:07:55.527
It also has no headphone jack

00:07:55.527 --> 00:07:57.576
which I honestly don't care.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:59.145
Life if you still think

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.747
that you need a headphone jack,

00:08:00.747 --> 00:08:02.104
I don't know that's not my problem

00:08:02.104 --> 00:08:02.949
that's your problem.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:05.304
Because I have completely done away

00:08:05.304 --> 00:08:07.025
with any corded headphones.

00:08:07.025 --> 00:08:08.875
The only time that I need
to use a corded headphone

00:08:08.875 --> 00:08:10.871
is when I'm making videos like this

00:08:10.871 --> 00:08:12.530
and I have to monitor audio.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:13.396
So that's really it.

00:08:13.396 --> 00:08:15.671
There is a slight bit of lag though,

00:08:15.671 --> 00:08:18.332
I will say that is extremely upsetting

00:08:18.332 --> 00:08:19.856
sometimes when I am editing

00:08:19.856 --> 00:08:21.621
but a lot of my editing

00:08:21.621 --> 00:08:23.450
I've sort of changed the way that I edit.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.365
I edit mostly looking at waveforms

00:08:25.365 --> 00:08:26.557
but even when I was one my desktop

00:08:26.557 --> 00:08:28.456
I feel like that's how
you sort of should edit.

00:08:28.456 --> 00:08:30.611
Yes you can edit to the
sound that you hear,

00:08:30.611 --> 00:08:31.842
but even then I feel like you're not

00:08:31.842 --> 00:08:33.591
gonna get the precise edits that you need.

00:08:33.591 --> 00:08:35.044
Feel free to fight about
it in the comments.

00:08:35.044 --> 00:08:37.214
Headphone jack, or no headphone jack?

00:08:37.214 --> 00:08:39.478
Again either way it doesn't
really effect me so,

00:08:39.478 --> 00:08:41.933
I will keep on living my
life headphone jack free.

00:08:41.933 --> 00:08:43.235
It has an eight core CPU

00:08:43.235 --> 00:08:44.658
plus seven core GPU.

00:08:44.658 --> 00:08:48.244
This is faster then
92% of all portable PCs

00:08:48.244 --> 00:08:50.422
that were sold in the past 12 months.

00:08:50.422 --> 00:08:52.169
I thought that was kind of
an interesting statistic.

00:08:52.169 --> 00:08:54.202
They also made a dig at Xbox.

00:08:54.202 --> 00:08:56.022
I was like, oh burn.

00:08:56.022 --> 00:08:57.160
They were talking about how fast

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.141
the graphics processor is in the iPad

00:08:59.141 --> 00:09:00.496
compared to the Xbox.

00:09:00.496 --> 00:09:01.891
Those are fighting words.

00:09:01.891 --> 00:09:04.141
The iPad Pro also has USBC,

00:09:05.021 --> 00:09:08.284
and it has charging out so
you can charge your iPhone

